    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-09T21:18:45+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-09T21:18:45+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T10:48:45Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T10:48:45Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough and cold front clear to the east of the state state overnight, as a high pressure system briefly establishes in the north on Saturday. Another series of troughs and cold fronts are expected to enter western SA early on Sunday, crossing the state and then clearing in the east by the end of Monday. A ridge of high pressure will then push into western SA on Monday before the associated high moves into waters south on Tuesday. A trough over the WA/NT border will also extend into SA at times from Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <warning-summary type="fire_weather_warning" start-time-local="2026-10-09T04:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-08T17:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">Fire Weather Warning for the North East Pastoral fire weather district for Friday</warning-summary>
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-09T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the afternoon and evening. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly in the early morning then tending east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 33.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening, possibly severe with damaging winds west of Leigh Creek. Winds northeast to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h in the middle of the day then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds east of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending south to southwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Leigh Creek, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
